{"id":15,"jsonrpc":"2.0","result":[{"detail":"t","documentation":"Return the same-type absolute value of any numeric primitive.\nSigned integer minimum raises checked Runtime failure; float abs clears the sign bit.\n\nReturns: Magnitude of type t, including positive zero for either floating zero.","kind":3,"label":"abs","textEdit":{"newText":"abs","range":{"end":{"character":18,"line":2},"start":{"character":18,"line":2}}}},{"detail":"t","documentation":"Return the principal inverse cosine in radians for an f32/f64 value.\n\nReturns: Type t angle in [0, pi]; outside the domain or NaN returns NaN.","kind":3,"label":"acos","textEdit":{"newText":"acos","range":{"end":{"character":18,"line":2},"start":{"character":18,"line":2}}}},{"detail":"t","documentation":"Return the principal inverse sine in radians for an f32/f64 value.\n\nReturns: Type t angle in [-pi/2, pi/2]; outside the domain or NaN returns NaN.","kind":3,"label":"asin","textEdit":{"newText":"asin","range":{"end":{"character":18,"line":2},"start":{"character":18,"line":2}}}},{"detail":"t","documentation":"Return the principal inverse tangent in radians for an f32/f64 value.\n\nReturns: Same-precision angle in [-pi/2, pi/2]; NaN propagates.","kind":3,"label":"atan","textEdit":{"newText":"atan","range":{"end":{"character":18,"line":2},"start":{"character":18,"line":2}}}},{"detail":"t","documentation":"Return a quadrant-aware f32/f64 angle in radians, with y first and x second.\nSigned origins, axes and infinities follow y's sign and typed pi subdivisions.\n\nReturns: Type t angle in [-pi, pi]; either NaN propagates.","kind":3,"label":"atan2","textEdit":{"newText":"atan2","range":{"end":{"character":18,"line":2},"start":{"character":18,"line":2}}}},{"detail":"t","documentation":"Round an f32 or f64 toward positive infinity, retaining floating precision.\n\nReturns: Integral floating value of type t, preserving negative zero.","kind":3,"label":"ceil","textEdit":{"newText":"ceil","range":{"end":{"character":18,"line":2},"start":{"character":18,"line":2}}}},{"detail":"t","documentation":"Constrain a numeric value to inclusive same-type bounds.\nNaN or reversed bounds raise checked Runtime failure before NaN input propagates.\n\nReturns: The input or selected endpoint, retaining type t.","kind":3,"label":"clamp","textEdit":{"newText":"clamp","range":{"end":{"character":18,"line":2},"start":{"character":18,"line":2}}}},{"detail":"t","documentation":"Return the cosine of an f32/f64 angle in radians.\n\nReturns: Same-precision cosine; NaN and either infinity produce NaN.","kind":3,"label":"cos","textEdit":{"newText":"cos","range":{"end":{"character":18,"line":2},"start":{"character":18,"line":2}}}},{"detail":"t","documentation":"Convert f32/f64 radians to degrees using pi rounded to the input precision.\n\nReturns: Type t degrees, computed as value times (180 / pi); finite scaling may overflow or underflow.","kind":3,"label":"degrees","textEdit":{"newText":"degrees","range":{"end":{"character":18,"line":2},"start":{"character":18,"line":2}}}},{"detail":"f32","documentation":"Euler's number rounded to f32.","kind":21,"label":"e_f32","textEdit":{"newText":"e_f32","range":{"end":{"character":18,"line":2},"start":{"character":18,"line":2}}}},{"detail":"f64","documentation":"Euler's number rounded to f64.","kind":21,"label":"e_f64","textEdit":{"newText":"e_f64","range":{"end":{"character":18,"line":2},"start":{"character":18,"line":2}}}},{"detail":"t","documentation":"Raise e to an f32/f64 exponent using the target's standard math facility.\n\nReturns: Type t result; negative infinity gives positive zero, positive infinity/overflow gives infinity, NaN propagates.","kind":3,"label":"exp","textEdit":{"newText":"exp","range":{"end":{"character":18,"line":2},"start":{"character":18,"line":2}}}},{"detail":"t","documentation":"Raise two to an f32/f64 exponent using the target's standard math facility.\n\nReturns: Type t result; negative infinity gives positive zero, positive infinity/overflow gives infinity, NaN propagates.","kind":3,"label":"exp2","textEdit":{"newText":"exp2","range":{"end":{"character":18,"line":2},"start":{"character":18,"line":2}}}},{"detail":"t","documentation":"Round an f32 or f64 toward negative infinity, retaining floating precision.\n\nReturns: Integral floating value of type t; use an explicit checked as for integers.","kind":3,"label":"floor","textEdit":{"newText":"floor","range":{"end":{"character":18,"line":2},"start":{"character":18,"line":2}}}},{"detail":"t","documentation":"Find an unclamped fraction along a finite, nondegenerate f32/f64 segment.\n\nReturns: Type t fraction; nonfinite inputs or equal endpoints return NaN; extrapolation may overflow.","kind":3,"label":"inverse_lerp","textEdit":{"newText":"inverse_lerp","range":{"end":{"character":18,"line":2},"start":{"character":18,"line":2}}}},{"detail":"bool","documentation":"Test an f32 or f64 value for finiteness.\n\nReturns: False for NaN and either infinity; true for zero and subnormal values.","kind":3,"label":"is_finite","textEdit":{"newText":"is_finite","range":{"end":{"character":18,"line":2},"start":{"character":18,"line":2}}}},{"detail":"bool","documentation":"Test an f32 or f64 value for either infinity.\n\nReturns: True for positive or negative infinity; false for NaN.","kind":3,"label":"is_infinite","textEdit":{"newText":"is_infinite","range":{"end":{"character":18,"line":2},"start":{"character":18,"line":2}}}},{"detail":"bool","documentation":"Test an f32 or f64 value for NaN.\n\nReturns: True exactly for NaN; payload and sign are not inspected.","kind":3,"label":"is_nan","textEdit":{"newText":"is_nan","range":{"end":{"character":18,"line":2},"start":{"character":18,"line":2}}}},{"detail":"t","documentation":"Interpolate or extrapolate finite f32/f64 values without clamping the weight.\nValidation precedes exact endpoint returns; interior weights give a finite in-range value.\n\nReturns: Type t result; any nonfinite input returns NaN, and extrapolation may overflow.","kind":3,"label":"lerp","textEdit":{"newText":"lerp","range":{"end":{"character":18,"line":2},"start":{"character":18,"line":2}}}},{"detail":"t","documentation":"Return the natural logarithm of an f32/f64 value.\n\nReturns: Type t logarithm; either zero gives negative infinity, negative values give NaN, NaN propagates.","kind":3,"label":"log","textEdit":{"newText":"log","range":{"end":{"character":18,"line":2},"start":{"character":18,"line":2}}}},{"detail":"t","documentation":"Return the base-two logarithm of an f32/f64 value.\n\nReturns: Type t logarithm; either zero gives negative infinity, negative values give NaN, NaN propagates.","kind":3,"label":"log2","textEdit":{"newText":"log2","range":{"end":{"character":18,"line":2},"start":{"character":18,"line":2}}}},{"detail":"t","documentation":"Select the larger of two values of one exact numeric primitive type.\n\nReturns: Same-type maximum; zero ties select positive zero if present.","kind":3,"label":"max","textEdit":{"newText":"max","range":{"end":{"character":18,"line":2},"start":{"character":18,"line":2}}}},{"detail":"t","documentation":"Select the smaller of two values of one exact numeric primitive type.\n\nReturns: Same-type minimum; zero ties select negative zero if present.","kind":3,"label":"min","textEdit":{"newText":"min","range":{"end":{"character":18,"line":2},"start":{"character":18,"line":2}}}},{"detail":"f32","documentation":"Pi rounded to f32; angles in the math module use radians.","kind":21,"label":"pi_f32","textEdit":{"newText":"pi_f32","range":{"end":{"character":18,"line":2},"start":{"character":18,"line":2}}}},{"detail":"f64","documentation":"Pi rounded to f64; angles in the math module use radians.","kind":21,"label":"pi_f64","textEdit":{"newText":"pi_f64","range":{"end":{"character":18,"line":2},"start":{"character":18,"line":2}}}},{"detail":"t","documentation":"Raise an f32/f64 base to a same-type real floating exponent.\nZero exponents and positive-one bases yield one before NaN handling; overflow yields infinity.\n\nReturns: Type t power; zero/infinity signs follow odd integral exponents, invalid real domains return NaN.","kind":3,"label":"pow","textEdit":{"newText":"pow","range":{"end":{"character":18,"line":2},"start":{"character":18,"line":2}}}},{"detail":"t","documentation":"Convert f32/f64 degrees to radians using pi rounded to the input precision.\n\nReturns: Type t radians, computed as value times (pi / 180); finite scaling may overflow or underflow.","kind":3,"label":"radians","textEdit":{"newText":"radians","range":{"end":{"character":18,"line":2},"start":{"character":18,"line":2}}}},{"detail":"t","documentation":"Round an f32 or f64 to nearest integral value, with halfway ties to even.\n\nReturns: Same-precision floating result; a result of zero retains the input sign.","kind":3,"label":"round","textEdit":{"newText":"round","range":{"end":{"character":18,"line":2},"start":{"character":18,"line":2}}}},{"detail":"t","documentation":"Return a numeric value's sign in its original type.\n\nReturns: Same-type negative one, zero or one; unsigned returns zero/one, floats retain NaN and zero sign.","kind":3,"label":"sign","textEdit":{"newText":"sign","range":{"end":{"character":18,"line":2},"start":{"character":18,"line":2}}}},{"detail":"t","documentation":"Return the sine of an f32/f64 angle in radians.\n\nReturns: Same-precision sine; NaN and either infinity produce NaN.","kind":3,"label":"sin","textEdit":{"newText":"sin","range":{"end":{"character":18,"line":2},"start":{"character":18,"line":2}}}},{"detail":"t","documentation":"Return the nearest principal square root of an f32/f64 value.\n\nReturns: Same-precision nonnegative root; negative nonzero values and NaN return NaN.","kind":3,"label":"sqrt","textEdit":{"newText":"sqrt","range":{"end":{"character":18,"line":2},"start":{"character":18,"line":2}}}},{"detail":"t","documentation":"Return the tangent of an f32/f64 angle in radians.\n\nReturns: Same-precision tangent; NaN and either infinity produce NaN.","kind":3,"label":"tan","textEdit":{"newText":"tan","range":{"end":{"character":18,"line":2},"start":{"character":18,"line":2}}}},{"detail":"f32","documentation":"One full turn in radians, rounded to f32 as twice pi_f32.","kind":21,"label":"tau_f32","textEdit":{"newText":"tau_f32","range":{"end":{"character":18,"line":2},"start":{"character":18,"line":2}}}},{"detail":"f64","documentation":"One full turn in radians, rounded to f64 as twice pi_f64.","kind":21,"label":"tau_f64","textEdit":{"newText":"tau_f64","range":{"end":{"character":18,"line":2},"start":{"character":18,"line":2}}}},{"detail":"t","documentation":"Round an f32 or f64 toward zero, retaining floating precision.\n\nReturns: Integral floating value of type t, preserving the input zero sign.","kind":3,"label":"trunc","textEdit":{"newText":"trunc","range":{"end":{"character":18,"line":2},"start":{"character":18,"line":2}}}}]}Content-Length: 326

